{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff"},"metadata":{"title":"ExponentialBackoff","externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExponentialBackoff.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff.swift#L26"},"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How long "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" waits before each new attempt at a batch that wasn’t delivered:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary exponential backoff, each nominal wait twice the one before, up to a maximum, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"jitter."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"title":"Waiting between attempts","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExponentialBackoff()"},{"text":" has nominal waits of 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 and 32 seconds, then 60 seconds for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every retry after that, with full jitter, as this one does:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let backoff = try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(1), maximumDelay: .seconds(60), jitter: .full)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/delay(beforeRetry:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is the nominal wait. What ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" sleeps before each retry","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"depends on the backoff’s jitter:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/full"},{"type":"text","text":", the default: a random wait, at least zero and less than the nominal one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drawn afresh before each retry from the destination’s random number generator."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/none","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": the nominal wait. It is exact when both delays count their attoseconds in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"53 significant bits or fewer, as any whole number of milliseconds under 295 seconds does;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise it is within about one part in 2⁵³ of it.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Jitter is on by default because apps tend to be refused all at once. A rate limiter’s window,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or an outage ending, refuses many apps at the same moment. Without jitter they would all retry","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at the same moments too, and each wave would be refused like the one before. Full jitter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spreads each wave over the whole wait. It also halves the average wait, so an app retries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"about twice as often during a long outage.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/SQ","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/SH","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/init(initialDelay:maximumDelay:jitter:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/init(jitter:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/initialDelay","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/jitter-swift.property","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/maximumDelay"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/delay(beforeRetry:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true},{"anchor":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDe